commit 420cd624512638572850631669674cbc7a8a629b
Author: MATTHEW M PEET <68134670+mmpeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 19:38:25 2026 -0700

    Vectorize int_2b's C3a assembly over the monomial-pair grid
    
    The assembly was a scalar loop over all m*n ordered monomial pairs -- m the
    product of A.ZR's per-direction monomial counts, n the same for B.ZL --
    calling num2cell, sub2ind and two fliplr on every iteration. It produced
    99.3% of the sub2ind calls in a composition profile: 186662 of them on one
    A'*A at degree 4, now 38.
    
    Every per-direction lookup depends on i and j only through IL(i,:) and
    IR(j,:), so each becomes a linear-index gather over the whole grid and the
    loop disappears. The mixed-radix condensation that sub2ind(fliplr(dims),
    num2cell(fliplr(idx)){:}) performed moves into the local 'condenseIdx',
    where the last direction carries stride 1 and direction k carries
    prod(dims(k+1:end)); it collapses to idx(1) at one direction and to 1 at
    none, the two cases the scalar version special-cased.
    
    Exact rather than merely equivalent: (i,k2a,k3a) -> row and (j,k3b) -> col
    are both bijections, so row recovers i and col recovers j, no two grid
    points emit the same triplet, and 'sparse' never sums a duplicate. Order of
    emission therefore cannot matter.
    
    One trap this hit on the way in, worth the guard it now carries: when
    C2b{k} is a ROW vector MATLAB returns a row for a column index, so
    'VV .* Ck(...)' implicitly expanded to an m*n by m*n matrix rather than
    failing. It surfaced as MATLAB:samelen from 'sparse' on 6 of 28
    shape/degree/product combinations. The value gather is now reshaped
    explicitly, as condenseIdx already was.
    
    Verified BIT-IDENTICAL: 28 captured A'*A and A'*B compositions over 7
    variable-group shapes at two degrees, 0.000e+00 relative difference against
    HEAD, with both captures written fresh; and all 28 shape/degree/product
    combinations construct.
    
    Un-profiled end-to-end, A'*A, mean +- std:
      deg3 dims[2 2]  m*n=5184     0.096+-0.043 -> 0.076+-0.020   noise-level
      deg4 dims[2 2]  m*n=186624   2.411+-0.043 -> 2.235+-0.054   1.08x
      deg5 dims[2 2]  m*n=1638400 23.02 +-0.42  -> 21.39 +-0.08   1.08x
    A profiled run makes int_2b look like 26-33% of mtimes and the change look
    like 1.27x-1.43x, but the profiler instruments each of the 186662 calls, so
    those figures are inflated; un-profiled the block is 7-8% and 1.08x is the
    honest number. The degree-5 case additionally checks out semantically:
    self-adjointness of A'*A at 1.08e-19 and the adjoint identity at 1.69e-21.
    
    161-check battery 0 failures; canonical-order sweep 0.00e+00 on 26 shapes x
    1120 orderings with its negative control detecting; LPI stability unchanged
    at ndec 462 with the same verdicts.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

