commit 9d5fdba813b760224c05c08ffb91d7943421d0c0
Author: MATTHEW M PEET <68134670+mmpeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 18:39:48 2026 -0700

    Memoise int_semisep's per-key results on the eight distinct factors
    
    The loop enumerates 11^ns3a (gamma,beta,alpha) triples and calls
    rearrangeCoef for each, but the eleven keys share only EIGHT distinct
    per-direction factors: the switch handles {111,212,313} in one branch and
    {221,331} in another. So Csep takes 8^ns3a values, not 11^ns3a, and the
    redundant rearrangeCoef calls are a factor (11/8)^ns3a -- 1.89x at two
    pass-through variables, 2.60x at three, 3.57x at four.
    
    Results are now cached on the representative tuple. On a hit both the
    Kronecker chain and the rearrangeCoef are skipped, which is why the walk
    computes the memo slot before building Csep rather than after. The size
    checks stay on the miss path, so every distinct Csep and Cnew is still
    validated exactly once.
    
    The duplicate factors are found by COMPARING the built Ci matrices, not by
    hard-coding the branch labels, so the grouping stays correct if the table
    or the domains change; the comparison is 11^2 per direction on matrices of
    a few dozen nonzeros. Representatives are then renumbered densely per
    direction so the memo is indexed in mixed radix over the distinct counts
    and holds prod(nCls) = 8^ns3a slots rather than 11^ns3a.
    
    Sharing one matrix across several output cells is safe under MATLAB's
    value semantics: the packed branch only reads it through find(), and the
    'separate' branch stores it, where copy-on-write makes aliasing
    unobservable. Both layouts are checked below.
    
    Verified BIT-IDENTICAL: int_semisep called directly against the pre-memo
    routine at ns3a 1/2/3, 0.0e+00 in BOTH the 'packed' and 'separate'
    layouts; and 28 captured A'*A and A'*B compositions through
    @sopvar/mtimes, 0.000e+00 relative difference against HEAD.
    
    Isolated: 1.11x at ns3a=1, 2.38x at ns3a=2, 6.27x at ns3a=3.
    End-to-end A'*A, 5 reps, mean +- std, at rand_sopvar's default density and
    at 0.25 -- note the earlier measurement in 22880a96 used density 1, the
    least favourable corner, and understated that change:
      out{w,y,z,m,n} deg3 dims[2 2] default  0.098+-0.024 -> 0.093+-0.024  1.06x
      out{w,y,z,m,n} deg3 dims[2 2] 0.25     0.150+-0.009 -> 0.138+-0.005  1.09x
      out{w,y,z,m,n} deg3 dims[4 4] default  0.096+-0.008 -> 0.082+-0.006  1.17x
      out{w,y,z,m,n} deg3 dims[4 4] 0.25     0.403+-0.008 -> 0.395+-0.007  1.02x
      out{y,z,m,n,p} deg2 dims[2 2] default  0.751+-0.007 -> 0.639+-0.015  1.18x
      out{y,z,m,n,p} deg2 dims[2 2] 0.25     2.655+-0.013 -> 2.592+-0.039  1.02x
    Peak memory costs +0.3 to +0.6 MB for the retained blocks, measured.
    
    161-check battery 0 failures; canonical-order sweep 0.00e+00 on 26 shapes
    x 1120 orderings with its negative control detecting; LPI stability
    unchanged -- same verdicts, ndec 462, and that test has ns3a = 1 where
    this change is worth nothing.
    
