commit 2f548d5b208563674639a8bd92448bb7dbad7c4c
Author: MATTHEW M PEET <68134670+mmpeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 03:38:21 2026 -0700

    Hoist the basis lift out of leftShiftMonomials_SS's coefficient loops
    
    S2 attempted Sec. 5.1's partial sum -- take the beta_a / alpha_b sum on
    the common basis BEFORE shifting the monomials, so the shift runs once
    per beta_b instead of once per (beta_a,beta_b). It was implemented,
    measured, and REJECTED as slower: 0.90x overall and 0.73x worst at
    nBetaA = nAlphaB = 9.
    
    The reason is worth recording, and is now a comment at the coefficient
    loop. Qmat compresses the monomial axis, NC <= NA*NB, so applying
    kron(speye(p),Qmat) first shrinks the rows from p*NA*NB to p*NC and the
    caller's sum afterwards adds the SMALLER matrices. Pre-summing instead
    accumulates the larger pre-shift matrix nI times, which is sparse
    accumulation in a loop -- the pattern CLAUDE.md warns about. So the
    document's ordering is a pessimization against this particular
    factorization, and the sum stays with the caller.
    
    What is kept from the attempt, all of it free:
    - kron(speye(p),Qmat) was rebuilt inside both loops, nI*nJ times
      identically. Hoisted; at nBetaA = nBetaB = 9 that is 81 constructions
      reduced to one.
    - The CA/CB cell shapes are checked once instead of inside the loops.
    - CC is preallocated rather than grown.
    
    Verified BIT-IDENTICAL: 28 captured A'*A and A'*B compositions over 7
    variable-group shapes at two degrees each, max relative difference
    0.000e+00 against the committed version. 161-check battery, 0 failures;
    canonical-order sweep 0.00e+00 on 26 shapes x 1120 orderings with its
    negative control detecting; LPI stability still straddles pi^2 = 9.8696
    at 462 decision variables. End-to-end timing is within run-to-run noise
    at the sizes measured (10-30 ms per composition); the removed work is
    redundant by construction rather than measurably faster here.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

