commit 28e0bd5134374a1aa0ab5ef0ee53b6311a56fe26
Author: MATTHEW M PEET <68134670+mmpeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 02:58:47 2026 -0700

    Sum the nMid diagonal blocks in mtimes_AT's PART 3
    
    Same change as 516e502a made to @sopvar/mtimes, applied to the vectorized
    sibling. PART 3 formed the whole nMid x nMid block product and masked off
    the diagonal, so it built three nMid^2-sized objects: the dense ones()
    inside Mask, spdiags(Mask(:)) of side numel(Mask), and -- on the decision
    path -- kron(K',I) of size (nMid^2*R*L) x (W*nMid*L). Sec. 5.4 of the
    sopvar document asks only for sum_d L_{jd} C R_{kd}.
    
    The A part is bit-identical to the masked form. The B part agrees to
    reassociation of the sum over d: exactly 0 at nMid==1 and ~2e-15 at
    nMid==4, which is summation order, not a different answer.
    
    This does NOT fully cure the memory blowup, and the header and PART 3 now
    say so. Degrees (2,3) complete where they previously wanted 122 GB, and
    the 158-check operation battery is green for the first time -- 161 checks,
    0 failures, with the S1{a,b} S2{y,z} S3{m,n} shape passing at 8.1e-16
    where it used to ask for 103.5 GB. But (3,3) still asks for 75.8 GB,
    because kron(Kd',I_L) has nnz(Kd)*left_BLCK_size entries -- it repeats Kd
    once per row of X_d -- so no matrix form of that map is small. That is a
    separate defect from the nMid^2 one fixed here. Applying it in bounded
    column chunks was tried and reverted: the chunk width collapses to one
    column in exactly the case that needs it, trading the memory blowup for
    right_BLCK_size sparse products. The fix is option 1 of the Note in
    Sec. 6.1.2 -- carry L and R in metadata and never form the product --
    which restructures how the decision block is propagated.
    
    Note this routine is called from nowhere in the toolbox; the live
    sdopvar path is @sdopvar/mtimes, which has no Mask/LeftMat structure and
    is untouched by this issue.
    
    Verified: unit test of both linear maps against the old formulas over
    nMid in {1,2,3,4}; the 9-cell degree sweep, 8 of 9 cells now completing
    and agreeing with @sopvar/mtimes to <=2.8e-15; 161-check battery over 7
    variable-group shapes, 0 failures.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

