commit 516e502a8f83bfff932dbc61b400466b6af9d9d8
Author: MATTHEW M PEET <68134670+mmpeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 01:53:39 2026 -0700

    Sum the nMid diagonal blocks in mtimes instead of masking a full product
    
    PART 4 of @sopvar/mtimes formed the whole nMid x nMid block product
    LeftMat*CMat*RightMat and then threw away every off-diagonal block with a
    mask, computing nMid^2 blocks to keep nMid of them. The mask itself held
    a DENSE ones(left_BLCK_size,right_BLCK_size).
    
    Sec. 5.4 of the sopvar document asks only for sum_d L_{jd} C R_{kd} --
    "efficient summation is all that is needed here" -- so the nMid diagonal
    blocks are now formed directly from block row d of LeftMat and block
    column d of RightMat. Mask, LeftMult and RightMult are gone.
    
    nMid is A.dims(2), the matrix dimension, so this scales with the operator
    rather than with the spatial variables; the removed dense ones() is
    L x R with L = dims(1)*NL_C and R = dims(2)*NR_C, and composition adds
    degrees, so NL_C outgrows both operands' bases.
    
    Verified: the two formulas agree BIT-IDENTICALLY (0.00e+00) across a
    sweep of nMid in {1,2,3,5,8} and block sizes, at 1.8-14x the speed; the
    158-check operation battery over 7 variable-group shapes is unchanged
    (its one failure is @sdopvar/mtimes_AT, untouched here and called from
    nowhere); the canonical-order sweep still gives 0.00e+00 on 26 shapes x
    1120 orderings with its negative control detecting; the LPI stability
    test still straddles pi^2 = 9.8696 at 462 decision variables. mtimes
    self time 0.126 -> 0.097 s on the profiled case, where nMid is only 2.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

