    Keep the zero-block parameter shorthand working through the reorder
    
    [] and scalar 0 stand for a zero parameter block throughout the class,
    but the canonical reorder indexed every cell unconditionally, so the
    shorthand threw MATLAB:badsubscript exactly when a permutation was
    needed and worked when it was not. Reproduced both ways before fixing.
    
    Skipped rather than special-cased: permuting a zero block is a no-op,
    and where a parameter really does hold one coefficient the gather can
    only be the identity, so skipping is exact in both cases.
    
    Verified: shorthand now constructs under a non-canonical declaration;
    158-check battery, canonical-order sweep and LPI stability unchanged.
    
