commit f226ae30265dd5f44045b23dbc04037cf1d6f251
Author: MATTHEW M PEET <68134670+mmpeet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 04:08:29 2026 -0700

    Fix the live sdopvar composition path and harden canonical_var_order
    
    An adversarial sweep over the canonical ordering confirmed that the
    alignment landed in the wrong places. @sopvar/mtimes and mtimes_AT both
    got it, but '*' on an sdopvar and an sopvar reaches
    mtimesSdopvarAndSopvar in @sdopvar/mtimes, and sopvar*sdopvar reaches it
    too via mtimes(B',A'); mtimes_AT is called from nowhere in the toolbox,
    so the fix was unreachable on the path that matters and every
    composition whose intermediate space had both a pass-through and a
    non-pass-through variable was still refused. Same block, applied there.
    
    Four ways canonical_var_order mishandled inputs the class supports
    elsewhere, all reproduced first:
    
    - Row-oriented exponent vectors hard-errored. canonicalize_multiplier
      normalizes bases with (:) precisely because callers pass rows, but the
      canonical reorder now runs before it, and monomial_gather matches
      degree-table ROWS, so a row basis widened the table and the 'rows'
      ismember threw. Normalized here too.
    - A repeated variable name silently truncated the operator: setdiff and
      intersect unique() their arguments, so the target list came back short
      and the gather dropped every direction past the duplicate. Now an
      error, as is a basis cell whose length disagrees with the variable
      list, which truncated the same way.
    - A domain containing NaN was rejected even when the caller passed the
      same array to both sides, because NaN ~= NaN.
    - An empty domain side given as [] rather than zeros(0,2) reached the
      pass-through comparison as 0x0 against 0x2 and threw a raw size error.
    
    The sweep's strongest result is a negative one: the permutation itself is
    correct. Two independent lanes rebuilt the same operator under different
    declared variable orders using genuine 3- and 4-cycles and unequal basis
    sizes per direction, and found 0 differing coefficients; a 738-evaluation
    kernel battery against the pre-change tree found the mtimes rejection and
    nothing else.
    
    Verified: 158 checks over 7 shapes, the live P*Q and (Q'*P')' now
    correct to 3e-16..2e-15 on all six shapes that fit in memory and to
    1.0e-15 on the seventh; canonical-order sweep still 0.00e+00 on 26
    shapes x 1120 orderings with its negative control detecting; LPI
    stability still straddles pi^2 = 9.8696 at 462 decision variables.
    
    Also corrected the vars.in/vars.out property documentation in both
    classdefs, which still claimed the names were stored SORTED -- [S2,S3]
    is sorted only when S2 is empty.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

